Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] J non-RPC complete-row replays; single-trial gate
 benches
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Card J t_01a1d862f6e2fc9e (design t_01a1d563 §3 J/§5). The component benches measured one signature at a
time and passed on the best of 3-5 trials. This adds whole-row replays of the measured streams through the
real code, run once (no best-of, no retry), with the budgets unchanged:

- tests/tui_gateway/test_j_nonrpc_rows.py: serve change_watcher + notification pollers <= 0.7% of a core
  (asserted for the gateway's 0.8% row too) over 600 s: every production watch with real frames to ten
  transports, the chg1 state stream, the hub's skill roots, two real _notification_poller_scoped_loop
  pollers (P1 run11: 1.85 serve / 1.17 gateway) with PollerStop deadlines, SQL, claims and custody, and the
  rf2 replica stream with the remote-index holder. Cells: base, tasks 5.8k/20k, replicas 40k, sessions 23k,
  all-max, all-max and base with a real >= 400 MiB WAL; each non-base cell <= 1.5x base. Zero span fallbacks
  (the P1 run11 ceiling). A RED control replays base without the reader deferral.
- tests/tui_gateway/test_j_nonrpc_producer_pid_rows.py: producer <= 0.2% (11 stores, sessions 5k/23k,
  checkpointed and >= 400 MiB WAL) and PID memo <= 0.05% (11 profiles, 300 lists, RECHECK_S backstop).
  Dimensions a path never reads are named as inapplicable in each docstring.
- The minutes-long cells run with J_ROWS_RUN=1 (operator benchmark); PID memo runs in the default suite.
- test_producer_admission_gate / test_status_pid_memo / test_watch_store_gate / test_notify_subs_gate:
  single trial instead of min-of-N; rates and thresholds unchanged.
- test_kanban_remote_index_defer: an absolute one-poll bound (a 1e9 DEFER_MAX_S mutant survived the
  relative tests); the no-holder cases as a table.

Measured at this tree (worker-5, load 19-40, one run each, 14 passed): rows 0.51-0.60% of a core, growth
<= 1.13x base, reader computes 0, 0 fallbacks, max notice latency 5.0 s; RED control 0.98% with 20 reader
computes. Producer 0.0095-0.0107%, PID memo 0.018%. Remote-index holder CPU (2.0-2.2% at 10k replicas,
8.3-10.0% at 40k) is recorded, not charged: design §3 books the remote index to H3. Gate mutation audit:
13 mutants, all RED.
